<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">guardian</ansi>

A guardian is a strategy role (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>): it fights as a fighter, and
steps in front of its ward to take a blow meant for them.

  <ansi fg="command">Tamsin Reed steps in front of you. (guard, 1 left)</ansi>

The blow then lands on the guardian instead, hit or miss, just as if it
had been aimed at them. The foe keeps its aim: its next blow comes at the
ward again.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Guards</ansi>

- A guardian has <ansi fg="yellow">2 guards</ansi> in each battle. Each blow it steps in for spends
  one.
- While any guard is spent, one comes back every <ansi fg="yellow">2 combat rounds</ansi>, up to 2.
  A new battle starts with both.
- Only weapon blows are guarded, not spells. A guardian keeps a healer's
  chant whole: the blow that might have broken it lands on the guardian
  (and may break the guardian's own chant, if it was chanting;
  <ansi fg="command">help interrupts</ansi>).
- A guardian steps in front of a foe's wound-up blow too, such as the
  forest ogre's Crushing Blow, and takes it (and its knockdown) itself.
- A guardian that is <ansi fg="yellow">knocked down</ansi> (2 rounds) or <ansi fg="yellow">stunned</ansi> (2 rounds) can't
  step in while it lasts (<ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi>), but keeps its guards. One that
  is down, fallen, or out of the fight guards no one.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The ward</ansi>

- Name a ward, and the guardian guards only them: while they are away or
  fallen, it guards no one. With none named, it guards whoever in your
  company is <ansi fg="yellow">most hurt</ansi> (the smallest share of their health left) and
  within its reach. Nobody hurt, nobody guarded: the guards are kept.
- A guardian must stand in its ward's <ansi fg="yellow">column, or the next one</ansi>, in the
  formation (<ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>). From further away it can't step in.
  <ansi fg="command">strategy</ansi> and <ansi fg="command">formation</ansi> warn you when a guardian stands too far from
  its ward. Someone not placed in the formation can guard, or be guarded,
  from anywhere.
- Several guardians may guard the same ward: the one nearest the front
  (then the left) steps in first. A guarded blow is never guarded again.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Commands</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">strategy [who] guard</ansi>          a guardian of whoever is most hurt
  <ansi fg="command">strategy [who] guard [other]</ansi>  a guardian of [other]: <ansi fg="command">strategy tamsin guard me</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">strategy [who] fighter</ansi>        back to fighting, the ward forgotten

[who] and [other] are <ansi fg="command">me</ansi>, or a companion by name (part of it will do) or
number (<ansi fg="command">#2</ansi>). <ansi fg="command">guardian</ansi> works in place of <ansi fg="command">guard</ansi>. You can be a
guardian yourself: <ansi fg="command">strategy me guard ysolde</ansi>.

As every strategy, a guardian and its ward are set before a battle; during
one they can be read but not changed. They are kept when you log out.

The battle summary counts each guardian's guards (<ansi fg="command">help battle-summary</ansi>).
In the web client, a guardian's menu in the Combat tab picks its ward, and
the battle view shows each guardian's guards left (<ansi fg="command">help webclient</ansi>).

Leaving a battle: <ansi fg="command">retreat [exit]</ansi> (or <ansi fg="command">flee</ansi>) prepares for one round,
then attempts to move the company together. See <ansi fg="command">help retreat</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help tactics</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
